//? Title: TrustRank: actual seeded Markov iterates
//? Subtitle: Actual native state, retained fixtures and explicit limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Ranking a linked network from trusted seed pages requires propagating mass
without treating every page as equally trusted. A personalized random surfer
repeatedly follows links while returning to the supplied seeds.
)

\toc

> The method

Let p be the seed distribution, including repeated-seed multiplicities. For a
dangling source, its entire link-following mass is redistributed through p. Each
iteration computes r_next=(1−α)p+αTᵀr, where T is row-stochastic after dangling
completion. For0≤α<1, the mapping contracts L1 distance by at mostα and has a
unique fixed point. With last successive difference δ, the returned fixed-point
error is bounded by αδ/(1−α). A finite iteration cap can leave an unresolved
result.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/trust_rank_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/trust_rank.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::trust_rank_work(2, {{0, 1}}, {0}, .5, 1e-12, 2, 3);
    std::print("| step | actual rank |\n|---:|---|\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < r.iterates.size(); ++i)
        std::print("|{}|`{}`|\n", i, r.iterates[i]);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Seed mass [1,0]; alpha.5");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual updates", r.iterations));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual last rank {}", r.rank));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/trust_rank_tiny.svg");
}
```
