> Interpretation and limits

Trusted seeds are external judgments, not labels inferred by the algorithm. The
rank is not a probability of honesty. Duplicate directed edges affect transition
probabilities; duplicate seeds affect personalization. The legacy vector wrapper
returns the same final iterate, while the new work API exposes convergence.

Every figure is saved locally by its complete editable program. No separate
reconstruction supplies algorithm state. Counters describe the selected events,
not elapsed time or peak memory.

> References

- [Gyongyi, Garcia-Molina and Pedersen, Combating Web Spam with TrustRank|https://www.vldb.org/conf/2004/RS15P3.PDF]

